keep: f9e520b1527c6f4c900411f90f0eada18fabe063 no-mistakes(ci): Only one of the 7 failing checks is caused by this PR: Behavior portable parallel 1. I fixed it. The other 6 fail the same way on PRs 38 and 42, which share this base (upstream-lean 9ed80766) without these changes, so I left them alone. **Caused by this PR (fixed).** tests/fm-pi-primary-types.test.sh failed with TS2339 "Property 'prompt' does not exist on type 'BeforeAgentStartEvent'" at fm-branch-supervision.ts:1684 and fm-primary-pi-watch.ts:1203. - Rule that broke: the Pi extensions must handle every before_agent_start event the installed Pi can raise. Pi 1.x also raises it for custom messages, which carry no prompt. - Cause: commit 9c86a2e0 cut PR 34's Pi 1.x narrowing after measuring only the locally installed Pi 0.85.0. CI installs the latest Pi without a version pin, which is now 1.3.0. - Every place that rule applies: the before_agent_start handlers in fm-branch-supervision.ts and fm-primary-pi-watch.ts, the sentence in docs/pi-supervision-branch.md that describes them, and the Pi event fixtures in tests/fm-pi-branch-extension.test.sh and tests/fm-pi-watch-extension.test.sh. - Fix: reverse-applied 9c86a2e0's patch for just those 5 paths, following the manifest's rule to recover a cut by its patch. The 2 extensions and 2 tests now equal 9ed80766's. The supervision-host quarantine stays cut. **Measured on this machine** (Pi 1.3.0 installed into a temp prefix and passed as FM_PI_PACKAGE_DIR; nothing installed globally): - Typecheck, upstream's files: exit 1 on Pi 1.3.0, exit 0 on Pi 0.85.0. - Typecheck, this head: passes on both Pi 1.3.0 and Pi 0.85.0. - fm-pi-branch-extension on Pi 1.3.0: run against upstream's extension it exits 1 with "TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'trim')" at fm-branch-supervision.ts:1686. On this head it exits 0 (51 checks). - fm-pi-watch-extension on Pi 0.85.0: exit 0 (60 checks) when run alone. One check failed once while it ran alongside the branch suite; it passed on the solo rerun. - fm-lint on the two changed tests: exit 0. fm-doc-audience-check: ok. git diff --check: clean. **Drift guard.** - drift-proof.txt now lists e3bca491 and moves `after:` to e3bca491, so it accepts only the commit that carries this change. - drift-measurements.txt gains "CI1 Pi 1.x narrowing" and "CI1 finalization" sections. - On an unreferenced scratch commit of this exact tree on top of e3bca491, the required check `bash bin/fm-drift-nightly.sh check --no-fetch --upstream 7df545bf74ff729ed1733f77b0aea02a9b164ac1` exits 0. It prints zero path-drift and carried-unproven lines, 25 pending lines naming .agent-config-dtjsb, and keep for e3bca491 and the scratch commit. It also prints the same 35 unproven cut commits that e3bca491's own check prints. - The same scratch commit checked against the old manifest exits 1, with path-drift for all 7 changed files. - The commit must sit directly on e3bca491 for the `after:` line to select it. **Not caused by this PR (no change).** Each also fails on PR 42 (run 39108950894) and/or PR 38 (run 39109282470) at the same base, in code this PR does not touch. They only moved between shards because this PR changes which files and tests exist. - Lint 2: SC2034 in bin/fm-pr-queue-sweep.sh:247 and SC2100 in tests/fm-pr-check-security.test.sh:5167. - Serial 8: fm-backlog-atomicity, already declined as F5. - Serial 9: fm-teardown, already declined as F6. Also fm-watch-arm's state-gone case, which fails on PR 38 too. - Serial 3: fm-gotmp. - Serial 1: fm-watch-triage; its failing assertion changes from run to run. - Serial 6: fm-pr-check-security, and fm-pr-made-with. bin/fm-pr-made-with.sh:167 uses a jq object value `{body: A + B}` that CI's jq 1.7 rejects; the local jq 1.8.2 accepts it. The PM's earlier decision assigned the post-cut upstream-lean commits to .agent-config-dtjsb, so I left these reds for that bead
